  "verification": "Exact installed-byte software checks cover all four canonical firmware images, native ignition scheduling and return ABI, launch episode and protective eligibility, read-only diagnostic checks and accepted-sample recovery, unchanged fuel-stage behavior, configured predecessor upgrade/removal, checksums and full-stack composition. Bench and vehicle validation remain required; no physical timing or DTC result is claimed.",
  "title": "Ignition Cut",
  "user_description": "Independent ignition-cut limiter with RPM hysteresis and optional injector pulse width. Provides the shared cut engine and combustion-observation recovery used by Launch Control V12.",
  "description": "Ignition Cut V10 with independent standalone and launch requests, hysteresis and fixed IPW. E847.0/.1/.2 are real cut requests; E848.0/.1 track fresh front samples and .2/.3 fresh rear samples where fitted. Active cuts freeze complete trim, mixture and observation transactions. Learning resumes after a native accepted front sample; catalyst observation also requires a fresh rear sample. Native FD30.1 fallback, electrical monitoring, previous misfire/shutdown evidence and completed catalyst results remain effective. No invented recovery timer is used. New compatible revision initializes E849=C0 once with E847/E848. Electrical coil-monitor eligibility remains native. The Ignition Cut-owned sample publication guard uses a short serialized check and keeps samples pending until the timing owner publishes release. Combustion observation uses a separately qualified Launch V12 timing episode (E849=C3); initialized held episodes refresh launch input and protection gates before suppressing observations. Genuine fallback, fault history and completed monitor results remain native.",
